    "done_when": "A type-6 differential SensorMapping no longer carries efm_index -1, which Python reads as the last positioned loop. Either efm_index becomes None for it, with the field typed int or None and every consumer handling None, or every consumer that indexes or matches by efm_index refuses or skips a mapping whose indices_differential is set. The consumers to cover are _apply_flux_loop_position_declarations in imas_ambix/data/geometry_adapter.py, the non-unique-claim pass in imas_ambix/gs/geometry.py, row_of_loop in imas_ambix/gs/operator.py, and the efm_index matching in imas_ambix/spine_bench/transform_geometry_source.py and imas_ambix/gs/artifact_geometry.py. The fragment lists each consumer with its verdict. A position declaration naming a differential channel raises GeometryAdapterError, pinned by a new test with a synthetic three-loop geometry table plus one type-6 mapping. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set) or all_debug, with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/maps-staging/jtmm-differential-loop-consumers, uv run --no-sync pytest tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/gs/test_operator.py tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py tests/gs/test_artifact_geometry.py tests/spine_bench/test_transform_geometry_source.py tests/spine_bench/test_machine_artifact_arm.py exits 0, captured once to a log with the revision and command on its first lines, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
